From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep i386 images below 4 GiB on the PS5.

Since 0600, map_view gives an allocation free to go anywhere from the
high reserved area at 0x1000000000 first. A relocatable i386 exe whose
preferred base was taken reached that last resort and was mapped there;
the guest saw its base truncated to 32 bits, and RtlImageNtHeader on it
faulted before the program started. An i386 image's limit is now 4 GiB,
so its last resort is the low reserved areas, as before 0600.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 17160e976c..08e048d798 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3598,6 +3598,12 @@ static NTSTATUS map_image_view( struct file_view **view_ret, struct pe_image_inf
 
     limit_low = max( limit_low, (ULONG_PTR)address_space_start );  /* make sure the DOS area remains free */
     if (!limit_high) limit_high = (ULONG_PTR)user_space_limit;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* An i386 image only runs below 4 GiB. When its preferred base is taken,
+     * the last resort below is any address, which map_view gives from the
+     * high reserved area first (0600). */
+    if (image_info->machine == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386) limit_high = min( limit_high, limit_4g - 1 );
+#endif
 
     /* first try the specified base */
 
